n 2026-07-31 MiniMax H3：打破任务和模态的边界今天，我们正式发布 MiniMax H3。这是一款通用的全模态生成模型，支持对文本、图像、视频、声音组成的多模态上下文的统一理解能力、能够输出具备原生双声道的音视频，最高可支持 15s 2K 分辨率。阅读更多 cite19†AIM3 2026-06-09 MaxProof: 生成式验证强化学习驱动的数学证明进化系统在 M3 发布推文中，我们汇报了 M3 模型在 IMO 2025 与 USAMO 2026 两组国际数学竞赛真题上的表现：在搭配 MaxProof 框架后，M3 均超过了人类金牌线。本文将进一步展开我们在推进数学证明能力过程中的技术路径，包括基座模型能力增强、verifier 对齐、refinement 能力构建，以及测试时增强框架 MaxProof 的设计。阅读更多 cite20†AIM3 2026-06-01 MiniMax M3：前沿 Coding 能力，1M上下文，原生多模态，一个模型全给你编程和智能体任务上达到了前沿的能力。它是一个使用全新注意力架构 MSA （MiniMax Sparse Attention ），最高支持 1M 超长上下文。 同时，如外界所期待的那样，它也是一个原生多模态模型。阅读更多 cite21†AI大模型2026-05-25为什么MiniMax大模型不认识\"马嘉祺\"？Minimax内部排查稀疏 Token 遗忘问题的记录MiniMax M2 系列受到了开发者社区的广泛关注，不少用户在深度使用中发现了一些 corner case——其中\"模型无法说出马嘉祺\"这个问题引发了较多讨论。本文详细记录了Minimax团队的内部排查过程，从 tokenizer 对齐到 lm_head 退化分析，揭示了稀疏 Token 遗忘的机制及修复方案。阅读更多 cite22†AIAgent 2026-04-27 MiniMax Agent Team: 为长程任务，持续进化而生今天我们介绍 MiniMax Agent 的整体升级，我们将升级后的 Agent 起了个新名字：Mavis — MiniMax as a Jarvis，你的 AI 管家。阅读更多 cite23†AIM2.7 2026-03-18 MiniMax M2.7: 开启模型的自我进化在 M2 系列模型发布后的几个月，我们收到了大量热心用户的反馈和建议，这促使我们进一步加速模型的迭代效率。除了更加认真工作之外，我们能找到的唯一途径就是开启模型和组织的自我进化。MiniMax M2.7是我们第一个模型深度参与迭代自己的模型。阅读更多 cite24†AI强化学习2026-02-12 Forge: 可扩展的 Agent 强化学习框架与算法把强化学习推到真实世界的 Agent 上,会撞到一个三角约束:系统吞吐、训练稳定性、Agent 灵活性三者互相拉扯,长期阻碍着大规模 RL 在工业级系统中的落地。阅读更多 cite25†AILLM 2026-02-12 MiniMax M2.5: 更快更强更智能，为真实世界生产力而生今天我们来介绍 MiniMax-M2.5。经过数十万个真实复杂环境中的大规模强化学习训练，M2.5 在编程、工具调用和搜索、办公等生产力场景都达到或者刷新了行业的 SOTA，比如 SWE-Bench Verified（80.2%），Multi-SWE-Bench（51.3%），BrowseComp（76.3%）。M2.5 优化了模型对复杂任务的拆解能力和思考过程中 token 的消耗，使其能更快地完成复杂的 Agentic 任务，比如在 SWE-Bench Verified 的测试中，比上一个版本 M2.1 完成任务的速度快了 37%。阅读更多 cite26†AIRole-Play 2026-01-28 MiniMax-M2-her 技术深度解析Worlds to Dream, Stories to Live｜一份关于如何在生产环境中构建真正可用的 Role-Play Agent 的技术报告。今年是我们做 Talkie / Xingye 的第三年。三年时间，足以让一个产品在用户生命中留下痕迹，也足以让我们从长期的使用反馈中读出一些不那么显而易见的洞见。阅读更多 cite27†AICoding 2025-12-23 MiniMax M2.1: 大幅提升多语言编程，为真实世界复杂任务而生MiniMax M2.1 系统性提升了 Rust、Java、Golang、C++ 等多编程语言能力，强化 Web/App 开发美学与复合指令约束，在 SWE-bench、VIBE 等基准上接近 Claude Opus 4.5 水平，并在 Claude Code、Cline、Roo Code 等主流 Agent 框架中展现稳定泛化表现，为真实世界复杂办公与编程任务提供高效解决方案。阅读更多 cite28†AIAgent 2025-10-27 MiniMax M2 & Agent，大巧若拙MiniMax正式开源并上线MiniMax M2，专为Agent和代码而生，仅Claude Sonnet 8%价格，2倍速度。模型具备顶级代码能力、强大Agentic表现和极致性价比，在Artificial Analysis榜单排名全球前五。同时推出MiniMax Agent产品，提供Lightning高效模式和Pro专业模式，限时免费开放使用。阅读更多 cite29†MiniMax-01开源模型2025-01-15 MiniMax-01开源：新架构开启Agent时代MiniMax发布开源MiniMax-01系列模型，包含Text-01和VL-01。采用线性注意力架构，4560亿参数459亿激活，400万Token上下文是GPT-4o的32倍，极致性价比1元/百万Token起。MiniMax阅读更多 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNew Released - Overview - Z.AI DEVELOPER DOCUMENT (https://docs.z.ai/release-notes/new-released)\nciteturn29423view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://docs.z.ai/release-notes/new-released\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 165\nL0: > ## Documentation Index\nL1: >\nL2: > Fetch the complete documentation index at: cite0†/llms.txt L3: >\nL4: > Use this file to discover all available pages before exploring further.\nL5: \nL6: cite1†Skip to main content L7: \nL8: cite2†Overview - Z.AI DEVELOPER DOCUMENT home page†z.ai L9: \nL10: Search...\nL11: \nL12: Navigation\nL13: \nL14: New Released\nL15: \nL16: cite3†Guides cite4†API Reference cite5†Coding Plan cite6†Released Notes cite7†Terms and Policy cite8†Help Center L17: \nL18: # New Released\nL19: \nL20: Follow along with updates across Z.AI’s models\nL21: \nL22: Copy page Copy page\nL23: ##\nL24: \nL25: cite9†​ L26: \nL27: Models\nL28: \nL29: cite10†​ L30: \nL31: [Button: 2026-08-26]\nL32: \nL33: GLM-5.3-Flash\nL34:   * Native visual capabilities enable the model to observe interfaces, rendering results, and interaction feedback—creating a closed loop across code, browsers, and GUIs.\nL35:   * Efficient hybrid architecture: Combines linear and sparse attention with 320B total parameters and 18B activated, significantly reducing compute and KV-cache requirements.\nL36:   * Beyond coding: Supports office document and financial research workflows, autonomously breaking down goals, using tools, and refining outputs. Learn more in our cite11†documentation .*\nL37: cite12†​ L38: \nL39: [Button: 2026-08-18]\nL40: \nL41: GLM-5.3\nL42:   * Stronger Coding Capabilities: GLM-5.3 delivers a significant improvement in coding capabilities, achieving a 50% gain over GLM-5.2 on Z.ai Code Bench and reaching state-of-the-art (SOTA) performance among open-source models on public benchmarks, including Terminal Bench 3.0.\nL43:   * Emergent Cybersecurity Capabilities: GLM-5.3 matches Mythos 5 in white-box code review and vulnerability discovery. In collaboration with multiple cybersecurity teams, it has been tested on real-world targets and has identified a total of 2,436 vulnerabilities, including 1,097 medium- and high-severity vulnerabilities.Learn more in our cite13†documentation .*\nL44: cite14†​ L45: \nL46: [Button: 2026-06-16]\nL47: \nL48: GLM-5.2\nL49:   * Supports 1M lossless context, significantly improving long-horizon task capabilities and reducing context drift and goal forgetting in complex tasks\nL50:   * Achieves open-source SOTA performance on coding and long-horizon task benchmarks, delivering more stable results in complex system engineering and deep debugging\nL51:   * Significantly improves the real-world developer experience, with more reliable project-level context handling, adherence to engineering standards, and multi-platform development. Learn more in our cite15†documentation .*\nL52: cite16†​ L53: \nL54: [Button: 2026-04-07]\nL55: \nL56: GLM-5.1\nL57:   * Designed for long-horizon tasks, GLM-5.1 can work independently for up to 8 hours in a single run, enabling a full loop from planning and execution to iterative refinement and final delivery.\nL58:   * It demonstrates stronger engineering intelligence across autonomous planning, sustained execution, bug fixing, and strategy iteration, while achieving comprehensive capability alignment with Claude Opus 4.6. Built with multi-turn SFT, RL, and a process-quality evaluation framework, GLM-5.1 further improves stability, consistency, and tool use over extended tasks. Learn more in our cite17†documentation .*\nL59: cite18†​ L60: \nL61: [Button: 2026-02-12]\nL62: \nL63: GLM-5\nL64:   * Designed for complex system engineering and long-range Agent tasks, GLM-5 shifts the paradigm from coding to engineering, demonstrating strong deep-reasoning performance in backend architecture, complex algorithms, and stubborn bug fixing.\nL65:   * It directly benchmarks against Claude Opus 4.5 in code-logic density and systems-engineering capability, and integrates DeepSeek Sparse Attention for higher token efficiency while preserving long-context quality.Learn more in our cite19†documentation .*\nL66: \nL67: cite20†​ L68: [Button: 2026-02-03]\nL69: \nL70: GLM-OCR\nL71:   * We’ve launched GLM-OCR, a compact and high-performance optical character recognition model powered by the self-developed CogViT and GLM-0.5B encoder-decoder architecture, enabling efficient cross-modal alignment through its dedicated connection layer.\nL72:   * The update leverages CLIP pre-training on billions of image-text pairs to deliver robust visual semantic understanding and key token extraction capabilities, while maintaining a lightweight design for fast inference. Learn more in our cite21†documentation .*\nL73: cite22†​ L74: \nL75: [Button: 2026-01-19]\nL76: \nL77: GLM-4.7-Flash\nL78:   * We’ve launched GLM-4.7-Flash, a lightweight and efficient model designed as the free-tier version of GLM-4.7, delivering strong performance across coding, reasoning, and generative tasks with low latency and high throughput.\nL79:   * The update brings competitive coding capabilities at its scale, offering best-in-class general abilities in writing, translation, long-form content, role play, and aesthetic outputs for high-frequency and real-time use cases. Learn more in our cite23†documentation .*\nL80: \nL81: cite24†​ L82: [Button: 2026-01-14]\nL83: \nL84: GLM-Image\nL85:   * We’ve launched GLM-Image, a state-of-the-art image generation model built on a multimodal architecture and fully trained on domestic chips, combining autoregressive semantic understanding with diffusion-based decoding to deliver high-quality, controllable visual generation.\nL86:   * The update significantly enhances performance in knowledge-intensive scenarios, with more stable and accurate text rendering inside images, making GLM-Image especially well suited for commercial design, educational illustrations, and content-rich visual applications.Learn more in our cite25†documentation .*\nL87: cite26†​ L88: \nL89: [Button: 2025-12-22]\nL90: \nL91: GLM-4.7\nL92:   * We’ve released GLM-4.7, our foundation model with significant improvements in coding, reasoning, and agentic capabilities. It delivers more reliable code generation, stronger long-context understanding, and improved end-to-end task execution across real-world development workflows.\nL93:   * The update brings open-source SOTA performance on major coding and reasoning benchmarks, enhanced agentic coding for goal-driven, multi-step tasks, and improved front-end and document generation quality. Learn more in our cite23†documentation .*\nL94: cite27†​ L95: \nL96: [Button: 2025-12-11]\nL97: \nL98: AutoGLM-Phone-Multilingual\nL99:   * We’ve launched AutoGLM-Phone-Multilingual, our latest multimodal mobile automation framework that understands screen content and executes real actions through ADB. It enables natural-language task execution across 50+ mainstream apps, delivering true end-to-end mobile control.\nL100:   * The update introduces multilingual support (English & Chinese), enhanced workflow planning capabilities, and improved task execution reliability. Learn more in our cite28†documentation .*\nL101: \nL102: cite29†​ L103: \nL104: [Button: 2025-12-10]\nL105: GLM-ASR-2512\nL106: \nL107:   * We’ve launched GLM-ASR-2512, our ASR model, delivering industry-leading accuracy with a Character Error Rate of just 0.0717, and significantly improved performance across real-world multilingual and accent-rich scenarios.\nL108:   * The update introduces enhanced custom dictionary support and expanded specialized terminology recognition. Learn more in our cite30†documentation .*\nL109: \nL110: cite31†​ L111: \nL112: [Button: 2025-12-08]\nL113: \nL114: GLM-4.6V\nL115:   * We’re excited to introduce GLM-4.6V, Z.ai’s latest iteration in multimodal large language models. This version enhances vision understanding, achieving state-of-the-art performance in tasks involving images and text.\nL116:   * The update also expands the context window to 128K, enabling more efficient processing of long inputs and complex multimodal tasks. Learn more in our cite32†documentation .*\nL117: \nL118: cite33†​ L119: \nL120: [Button: 2025-09-30]\nL121: \nL122: GLM-4.6\nL123:   * We’ve launched GLM-4.6, the flagship coding model, showcasing enhanced performance in both public benchmarks and real-world programming tasks, making it the leading coding model in China.\nL124:   * The update also expands the context window to 200K, improving its ability to handle longer code and complex agent tasks. Learn more in our cite34†documentation .*\nL125: \nL126: cite35†​ L127: \nL128: [Button: 2025-08-11]\nL129: \nL130: GLM-4.5V\nL131:   * We’ve launched GLM-4.5V, a 100B-scale open-source vision reasoning model, supporting a broad range of visual tasks including video understanding, visual grounding, GUI agents and etc.\nL132:   * The update also adds a new thinking mode. Learn more in our cite36†documentation .*\nL133: \nL134: cite37†​ L135: \nL136: [Button: 2025-08-08]\nL137: \nL138: GLM Slide/Poster Agent(beta)\nL139:   * We’ve launched GLM Slide/Poster Agent, an AI-powered creation agent that combines information retrieval, content structuring, and visual layout design to generate professional-grade slides and posters from natural language instructions.\nL140:   * The update also brings a seamless integration of content generation with design conventions. Learn more in our cite38†documentation .*\nL141: \nL142: cite39†​ L143: \nL144: [Button: 2025-07-28]\nL145: \nL146: GLM-4.5 Series\nL147:   * We’ve launched GLM-4.5, our latest native agentic LLM, delivering doubled parameter efficiency and strong reasoning, coding, and agentic capabilities.\nL148:   * It also offers seamless one-click compatibility with the Claude Code framework. Learn more in our cite40†documentation .*\nL149: \nL150: cite41†​ L151: \nL152: [Button: 2025-07-15]\nL153: \nL154: CogVideoX-3\nL155:   * We’ve launched CogVideoX-3, an incremental upgrade to our video generation model with improved quality and new features.\nL156:   * It adds support for start and end frame synthesis. Learn more in our cite42†documentation .*\nL157: \nL158: Was this page helpful?\nL159: \nL160: Yes No\nL161: \nL162: cite43†x†x.com cite44†github†github.com cite45†discord†discord.gg cite46†linkedin†www.linkedin.com L163: \nL164: cite47†Powered byThis documentation is built and hosted on Mintlify, a developer documentation platform†www.mintlify.com --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChange Log | DeepSeek API Docs (https://api-docs.deepseek.com/updates)\nciteturn29423view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/updates\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://api-docs.deepseek.com/updates/; Total lines: 399\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content L1: \nL2:   * cite1†Change Log L3: \nL4: [Button: On this page]\nL5: \nL6: # Change Log\nL7: \nL8: * * *\nL9: \nL10: ## Date: 2026-09-10cite2†​ L11: ### DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash Releasecite3†​ L12: \nL13: Today, we officially release the DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash model. It is the smallest model in our new architecture family, with native multimodal visual understanding. The new architecture is designed for a higher capability ceiling, faster inference, higher throughput, and scaling to larger models.\nL14:   * GPQA Diamond: 90.9\nL15:   * HLE: 36.8 (39.1*)\nL16:   * Codeforces (Rating): 3471\nL17:   * MathArena Apex: 65.6\nL18:   * Terminal-Bench 2.1: 90.6\nL19:   * Terminal-Bench 3.0: 30.0\nL20:   * Terminal-Bench 4.0: 31.2\nL21:   * DeepSWE v1.1: 74.2\nL22:   * ProgramBench: 20.3\nL23:   * NL2Repo-Bench: 65.4\nL24:   * CyberGym: 88.1\nL25:   * SEC-Bench Pro: 62.8\nL26:   * ExploitGym: 15.3\nL27:   * HLE (w/tools): 63.9\nL28:   * Automation-Bench: 54.8\nL29:   * Agents' Last Exam: 31.8\nL30:   * Chartography (w/tools): 78.9\nL31:   * BabyVision (w/tools): 89.6\nL32:   * ZeroBench-main (w/tools): 49.0\nL33: * Tested only on the pure-text subset of the HLE benchmark set.\nL34: \nL35: API changes\nL36: \nL37: DeepSeek V4.1 Flash is now available on the DeepSeek API with native multimodal support. Change the model name to `deepseek-flash` to call the latest V4.1 Flash model. The previous-generation models V4 Flash and V4 Flash Vision Exp have been retired; for compatibility, the model names `deepseek-v4-flash` and `deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp` are temporarily routed to V4.1 Flash.\nL38: In response to user demand, we have decided to continue providing API services for DeepSeek V4 Pro after September 14, 2026, with the billing method remaining unchanged. We will provide further notice should there be any changes. Thank you for your understanding and support!\nL39: \nL40: API pricing adjustment\nL41: \nL42: With the release of DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, API prices have been reduced accordingly. For details, please refer to cite4†Models & Pricing .\nL43: \nL44: For more details, please refer to cite5†this documentation .\nL45: \nL46: * * *\nL47: ## Date: 2026-08-21cite6†​ L48: ### DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Vision-Exp Releasecite7†​ L49: \nL50: Today, the new multimodal vision understanding model DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Vision-Exp is now available on the DeepSeek API platform. This is an experimental model that can be accessed by setting `model='deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp'`.\nL51: \nL52:   * Terminal Bench 2.1: 83.9\nL53:   * NL2Repo: 57.7\nL54:   * DeepSWE: 59.3\nL55:   * DSBench-Hard: 63.6\nL56:   * AutomationBench (Public): 25.7\nL57:   * ApexBench (Pass@1): 36.5\nL58:   * Agents' Last Exam: 27.3\nL59:   * Chartography: 64.3\nL60:   * ZeroBench (Pass@5): 35.0\nL61: * For the Code Agent text tasks in the public benchmark sets, the DeepSeek family models were tested using the DeepSeek Harness minimal mode as the framework, with the max effort level, topp=0.95, and temperature=1.0; in the ApexBench and Agents' Last Exam evaluations, the text model DeepSeek-V4-Flash ignores the multimodal elements within them.\nL62: \nL63: In terms of pure-text capabilities (agent, reasoning, world knowledge, etc.), DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Vision-Exp is on par with the official DeepSeek-V4-Flash.\nL64: On agent benchmarks that require visual understanding, DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Vision-Exp delivers a significant leap over DeepSeek-V4-Flash, bringing its multimodal agent capabilities close to Opus-4.8.\nL65: \nL66: For usage details, please refer to the cite8†Vision guide .\nL67: \nL68: * * *\nL69: ## Date: 2026-08-13cite9†​ L70: ### DeepSeek-V4-Pro Updatecite10†​ L71: \nL72: The GA release of DeepSeek-V4-Pro has been rolled out on the APP, Web, and API. The API calling method remains unchanged — simply set the model name to `deepseek-v4-pro` to use the latest version.\nL73: \nL74: Significantly enhanced Agent capabilities\nL75: \nL76: The GA version of DeepSeek V4 Pro greatly enhances agent capabilities, with particularly significant performance improvements in production environments.\nL77:   * HLE (wo / w tools): 42.7/60.0\nL78:   * Terminal Bench 2.1: 87.9\nL79:   * NL2Repo: 61.5\nL80:   * Cybergym: 83.3\nL81:   * DeepSWE: 62.7\nL82:   * Toolathlon-Verified: 74.1\nL83:   * Agents' Last Exam: 25.7\nL84:   * AutomationBench (Public): 31.8\nL85:   * DSBench-FullStack: 71.1\nL86:   * DSBench-Hard: 67.2\nL87: Native support for the Responses API\nL88: The DeepSeek API now natively supports the OpenAI Responses API format and is specifically adapted for Codex. Users can refer to the cite11†official documentation and complete the Codex configuration with a one-click configuration script.\nL89: \nL90: More flexible thinking effort control\nL91: The thinking modes of V4-Pro and V4-Flash now support three thinking effort levels: low / high / max. In real-world usage, users can flexibly choose based on task complexity: use low for simple tasks, high for daily Agent tasks, and max for more complex scenarios. For setup instructions, please refer to the official API documentation: cite12†Thinking Mode .\nL92: \nL93: API Pricing Adjustment\nL94: With the official release of the DeepSeek V4 model family, we will cite4†update and adjust API pricing . To allocate resources more reasonably, we will adopt peak/off-peak pricing, with off-peak prices set at half of the peak-hour prices, encouraging users to schedule their tasks based on actual usage. The new prices will take effect at 16:00 (UTC Time) on August 16, 2026.\nL95: \nL96: For more details, please refer to cite13†this documentation .\nL97: \nL98: * * *\nL99: ## Date: 2026-07-31cite14†​ L100: ### DeepSeek-V4-Flash Updatecite15†​ L101: \nL102: The official release of the DeepSeek-V4-Flash API is now in public beta. The API calling method remains unchanged — simply set the model name to `deepseek-v4-flash` to use the latest version.\nL103: \nL104: Significantly enhanced agent capabilities, with benchmark results far exceeding V4-Pro-Preview:\nL105:   * Terminal Bench 2.1: 82.7\nL106:   * NL2Repo: 54.2\nL107:   * Cybergym: 76.7\nL108:   * DeepSWE: 54.4\nL109:   * Toolathlon verified: 70.3\nL110:   * Agent Last Exam: 25.2\nL111:   * Automation Bench (Public): 25.1\nL112:   * DSBench-FullStack: 68.7\nL113:   * DSBench-Hard: 59.6\nL114: Note 1: For the Code Agent tasks in the public benchmark sets, the official DeepSeek-V4-Flash was tested using the DeepSeek Harness minimal mode (to be released soon) as the framework, with the max effort level, topp=0.95, and temperature=1.0\nL115: Note 2: DSBench-FullStack is an internal full-stack development test set, and DSBench-Hard is an internal Coding Agent hard-problem test set\nL116: The official V4-Flash natively supports the Responses API format and is specifically adapted for Codex. For the specific configuration, please refer to the cite11†documentation .\nL117: DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 keeps the same model architecture and size as DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Preview, and was only re-post-trained.\nL118: Note: This update only upgrades the DeepSeek-V4-Flash API. The DeepSeek-V4-Pro API and the APP/WEB models are unchanged.\nL119: The official release of DeepSeek-V4-Pro will follow soon.\nL120: \nL121: * * *\nL122: ## Date: 2026-04-24cite16†​ L123: ### DeepSeek-V4cite17†​ L124: \nL125: The DeepSeek API now supports V4-Pro and V4-Flash, available via both the OpenAI ChatCompletions interface and the Anthropic interface. To access the new models, the base_url remains unchanged, and the model parameter should be set to `deepseek-v4-pro` or `deepseek-v4-flash`.\nL126: The two legacy API model names, `deepseek-chat` and `deepseek-reasoner`, will be discontinued in three months (2026-07-24). During the current period, these two model names point to the non-thinking mode and thinking mode of `deepseek-v4-flash`, respectively.\nL127: \nL128: For more details, please refer to cite18†this documentation .\nL129: \nL130: * * *\nL131: ## Date: 2025-12-01cite19†​ L132: \nL133: ### DeepSeek-V3.2cite20†​ L134: \nL135: Both `deepseek-chat` and `deepseek-reasoner` have been upgraded to DeepSeek-V3.2.\nL136: \nL137:   * `deepseek-chat` corresponds to DeepSeek-V3.2's non-thinking mode\nL138:   * `deepseek-reasoner` corresponds to DeepSeek-V3.2's thinking mode\nL139: ### DeepSeek-V3.2-Specialecite21†​ L140: \nL141: DeepSeek-V3.2-Speciale is served via a temporary endpoint: base_url=\"cite22†https://api.deepseek.com/v3.2_speciale_expires_on_20251215†api.deepseek.com \". Same pricing as V3.2, no tool calls, available until Dec 15th, 2025, 15:59 (UTC Time).\nL142: \nL143: For more details, please refer to cite23†this documentation .\nL144: \nL145: * * *\nL146: \nL147: ## Date: 2025-09-29cite24†​ L148: ### DeepSeek-V3.2-Expcite25†​ L149: \nL150: Both `deepseek-chat` and `deepseek-reasoner` have been upgraded to DeepSeek-V3.2-Exp.\nL151: \nL152:   * `deepseek-chat` corresponds to DeepSeek-V3.2-Exp's non-thinking mode\nL153:   * `deepseek-reasoner` corresponds to DeepSeek-V3.2-Exp's thinking mode\nL154: \nL155: For more details, please refer to cite26†this documentation .\nL156: \nL157: * * *\nL158: \nL159: ## Date: 2025-09-22cite27†​ L160: ### DeepSeek-V3.1-Terminuscite28†​ L161: \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMoonshot AI · GitHub (https://github.com/MoonshotAI)\nciteturn29423view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/MoonshotAI\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 310\n"
